      "message": "As I mentioned offline, `zerocopy` crates helps you to transmute raw bytes into struct without any copy/modification/`unsafe`.\n\n- Define your struct with `#[derive(FromBytes)]` and use `LayoutVerified::new_from_prefix`.\n\ne.g. \nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/config.rs?q\u003dpvmfw%2Fsrc%2Fconfig.rs\u0026sq\u003drepo:android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\n\n\n- You can also explicitly annotate each fields whether their\u0027s little endian / big endian. U32\u003cBigEndian\u003e\n\ne.g. \nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/rust/crates/virtio-drivers/src/device/socket/protocol.rs;l\u003d51?q\u003df:rs$%20%5CbLittleEndian%5Cb\u0026sq\u003drepo:android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main",
